§ `reg 8(3): a relevant person for the purposes of a regulation`
-- src:251: an auction platform is a relevant person for the purposes of those provisions only.
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `credit institution`) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 27, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 24, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 27, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`) FALSE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 24, "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 24, "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`) TRUE NOTHING (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 24, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `auction platform`, `estate agent`) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 27, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` EMPTY TRUE (JUST FALSE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 24, "") EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` (LIST `casino`) TRUE (JUST TRUE) (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 27, "") EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `reg 8(3A) and (4)`
-- src:252: Regulation 29 applies to a customer provided with a pooled account by a relevant person.
#ASSERT `reg 8(3A) regulation 29 applies to the customer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(3A) regulation 29 applies to the customer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:253: the definitions in regulations 10 to 14 apply for the purposes of this regulation.
#ASSERT `reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 10, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 14, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 9, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 15, "") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` (`reg 8(3) Regulation` OF 14, "A") EQUALS NOTHING

§ `reg 9: carrying on business in the United Kingdom`
-- src:257-261: the second case.
#ASSERT `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:262-266: the third case.
#ASSERT `reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:269: for the second case it is irrelevant where the person with whom the business is carried on is situated.
#ASSERT `reg 9(5)(b) the second case, whatever the situation of the person with whom the business is carried on` TRUE TRUE FALSE `reg 9(5)(b) in the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(5)(b) the second case, whatever the situation of the person with whom the business is carried on` TRUE TRUE FALSE `reg 9(5)(b) outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(5)(b) the second case, whatever the situation of the person with whom the business is carried on` FALSE TRUE FALSE `reg 9(5)(b) in the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 9(5)(b) the second case, whatever the situation of the person with whom the business is carried on` FALSE TRUE FALSE `reg 9(5)(b) outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:255: regarded as carrying on business in the cases described, even if A would not otherwise be so regarded.
#ASSERT `reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Helpers: three-valued OR and AND`
-- OR: one JUST TRUE wins; all JUST FALSE is FALSE; anything else is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST NOTHING, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- AND: one JUST FALSE loses; all JUST TRUE is TRUE; anything else is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` (LIST NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
